From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] asahi: admit T8132 (M4, G16G) at the device-parameter gate

Revert the T8132 part of commit 2df99f490d3 ("Align host fixtures with
opt-in Air barriers and held M4 device admission"), which added
`params->chip_id == 0x8132` to the refusal in agx_params_driver_supported()
and flipped the matching tests.

Only the T8132 hunks are reverted:
- agx_chip.c: drop the `chip_id == 0x8132` refusal; the G16G branch below
  it still admits exactly chip 0x8132, one die, one cluster, AGX3 shaders
  and the HAL200 interface.
- test-chip-admission.c: the M4 (G16G) fixture is admitted again.
- test-chip.cpp: G16GAdmissionHeldForHardwareQualification is back to
  G16GRequiresExactKernelContract, as before 2df99f490d3.

Kept from 2df99f490d3: the G16G case in agx_chip_driver_supported(), the
T6040 (0x6040) refusal, and the G15G move to the wide-barrier cases in
test-agx3-packing.c.

Measured on the J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch M4, T8132) under the Aurora G16
kernel backend: GET_PARAMS reports G16G revision 0x10, chip 0x8132, one die,
one cluster of 10 cores, USC generation 3, HAL 200, features 0x1c02
(VM_STATUS, PER_COMMAND_INPUT_SYNCS, VM_STATUS_MIRROR, EXACT_PRIOR_BARRIERS),
which this gate admits.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/asahi/lib/agx_chip.c                  | 3 +--
 src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip-admission.c | 2 +-
 src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip.cpp         | 7 ++-----
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/asahi/lib/agx_chip.c b/src/asahi/lib/agx_chip.c
index da139589e67..23c850a6b18 100644
--- a/src/asahi/lib/agx_chip.c
+++ b/src/asahi/lib/agx_chip.c
@@ -283,8 +283,7 @@ agx_params_driver_supported(const struct drm_asahi_params_global *params)
       return false;
 
    const enum agx_chip chip = agx_chip_from_params(params);
-   if (!agx_chip_driver_supported(chip) || params->chip_id == 0x6040 ||
-       params->chip_id == 0x8132)
+   if (!agx_chip_driver_supported(chip) || params->chip_id == 0x6040)
       return false;
 
    switch (chip) {
diff --git a/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip-admission.c b/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip-admission.c
index 532be1c4964..453598ea639 100644
--- a/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip-admission.c
+++ b/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip-admission.c
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ main(void)
    m4.chip_id = 0x8132;
    m4.num_clusters_total = 1;
    assert(agx_chip_driver_supported(AGX_CHIP_G16G));
-   assert(!agx_params_driver_supported(&m4));
+   assert(agx_params_driver_supported(&m4));
 
    /* T8122 (G15G) is admitted by default for its exact identity and
     * supported legacy firmware/kernel contract. */
diff --git a/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip.cpp b/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip.cpp
index bf679869990..7b7539b9151 100644
--- a/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip.cpp
+++ b/src/asahi/lib/tests/test-chip.cpp
@@ -20,14 +20,11 @@ g16g_params()
    return params;
 }
 
-TEST(AGXChip, G16GAdmissionHeldForHardwareQualification)
+TEST(AGXChip, G16GRequiresExactKernelContract)
 {
    const drm_asahi_params_global valid = g16g_params();
    ASSERT_EQ(agx_chip_from_params(&valid), AGX_CHIP_G16G);
-   /* Retain compiler capability coverage, but this M3 update does not
-    * qualify an M4 device for opening. */
-   ASSERT_TRUE(agx_chip_driver_supported(AGX_CHIP_G16G));
-   ASSERT_FALSE(agx_params_driver_supported(&valid));
+   ASSERT_TRUE(agx_params_driver_supported(&valid));
    EXPECT_FALSE(agx_params_driver_supported(nullptr));
 
    for (unsigned field = 0; field < 7; ++field) {
-- 
2.43.0

